  "id": "electronics.analog-circuits.op-amp-circuits",
  "name": "Op-Amp Circuits",
  "level": "process",
  "parent": "electronics.analog-circuits",
  "description": "Design pedagogy for the operational amplifier, the most versatile analog IC: the ideal model (infinite gain, infinite input impedance, zero output impedance, virtual short under feedback), the canonical closed-loop topologies (inverting, non-inverting, follower, summing, difference), integration and differentiation, the comparator and Schmitt trigger with hysteresis, and active filters (first-order Sallen-Key low/high-pass and band-pass) that replace inductors with op-amp gain. Links passive-filter theory rather than re-deriving it.",
  "timeline": "Years 20-35",
  "outputs": [
    "op-amp-circuit-designs"
  ],
